Subject: [PATCH v6 10/10] jails/instances/lab-mail: Sync the whole Fastmail
 account
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: rqvvtqsnzoxqpqppunwpspvxrwplpvvk
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:13:13 +0000

Mail that lands outside the list's folders never reaches the other
side, so lab-mail is an incomplete copy of the account. A message that
Fastmail files into INBOX stays on Fastmail. A message that Dovecot
holds in INBOX never reaches Fastmail, because that INBOX sits outside
the maildir and outside the sync.

Syncing every folder makes lab-mail a full copy of the account. That
copy holds more than the list, though, and any login may read. The
ACL, not the sync, now keeps readers to the list.

- mbsync syncs every folder, and creates on lab-mail a folder that is
  new on Fastmail.
- INBOX is a folder of the maildir like the others.
- Readers may list and read only lists and Archive. Pat and mbsync
  keep their rights in every folder, and mbsync may create one.
